  "task_definition": "Directional pair: previously reported stored_text (premise) then candidate_text (hypothesis). expected_nli is a provisional textual classification. scope_compatible is same subject, predicate and non-disjoint time *regardless of assertion*. stored_claim_status is an explicitly synthetic admission assumption, not a lookup of PostgreSQL. memory_conflict_eligible means compatible scope AND an admitted asserted source, qualifying only for a potential Memory-domain review. expected_resolution distinguishes explicit corrections and tentative conversational resolution from Memory conflicts; it is not an executable command.",
  "policy_contracts": [
    "Tentative/uncertain source claims remain unadmitted to authoritative Memory.",
    "Subsequent definite user information may resolve tentative conversational state without creating an authoritative Memory conflict.",
    "A tentative new statement must not overwrite or silently supersede an existing admitted Memory record.",
    "Explicit user corrections use existing Memory-domain authorization and version controls independently of NLI softmax thresholds.",
    "NLI is advisory semantic evidence; Memory ownership controls admission, conflicts, correction and retraction."
  ],
  "limits": "Synthetic oracle source-admission and scope annotations are not an implemented classifier or memory policy. NLI 0.90 is fixed diagnostic only; do not tune on this corpus. Preserve v1 benchmark hash and do not pool v1 and v2 scores. Independent annotation and separate unseen holdout are required.",
